WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.397
Now we move into the cleaning section.

00:00:02.397 --> 00:00:08.807
This table is intentionally messy because real data frequently contains small inconsistencies that can create

00:00:08.807 --> 00:00:13.687
large analytical problems. Look at the channel column.

00:00:13.687 --> 00:00:21.292
We have values such as Web, EMAIL, web, and Store with inconsistent capitalization and spacing.

00:00:21.292 --> 00:00:24.432
The amount column contains currency symbols and also a missing value.

00:00:24.432 --> 00:00:26.797
One date is not a valid date.

00:00:26.797 --> 00:00:29.342
The city column has a missing value.

00:00:29.342 --> 00:00:34.762
And order ID one thousand three appears twice.

00:00:34.762 --> 00:00:35.527
None of these problems is unusual.

00:00:35.527 --> 00:00:41.072
The danger is that some of them are easy to miss.

00:00:41.072 --> 00:00:43.592
A duplicate can inflate revenue.

00:00:43.592 --> 00:00:48.397
Inconsistent categories can split one group into several fake groups.

00:00:48.397 --> 00:00:51.822
A bad date can break time-based analysis.

00:00:51.822 --> 00:00:56.272
Our goal is not to immediately start deleting or filling values.

00:00:56.272 --> 00:01:01.087
First we need to measure the problems and understand what each one means.

00:01:01.087 --> 00:01:05.177
Good data cleaning is not a sequence of automatic commands.

00:01:05.177 --> 00:01:08.402
It is a sequence of decisions supported by evidence.
